      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a decent start, but it feels a bit thin. For a \"Getting Started\" guide, I was hoping for a bit more depth on how to actually implement the request, maybe some specific error handling or configuration details.\n\nLow score warning though: our linter is actually flagging this version because the structural density is too low to meet our \"comprehensive\" threshold for the initial automated pass. It's a bit of a pain, but if the score is too low, it gets kicked back to us for manual review. \n\nCan you expand on the technical steps? Just... please keep it readable. Don't just add more headings or bullets for the sake of it, but it definitely needs more detail and more of those structural elements to hit the requirements.",
      "source": "evaluator"
